      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "08ed093a-1d8e-5375-bc48-ab71eedbfacd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walter Horten, Reimar Horten, Horten brothers\n- Products: Horten H.IX, Ho 229, Gotha Go 229\n- Companies: Gothaer Waggonfabrik\n- Organizations: RLM\n- Topics: German prototype fighter-bombers, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Walter Horten was born on 13 November 1913 and died on 9 December 1998 in Baden-Baden, Germany.\n- Reimar Horten was born on 12 March 1915 and died on 14 March 1994 in Villa General Belgrano, Argentina.\n- Walter Horten and Reimar Horten were German aircraft pilots and enthusiasts who were sometimes credited as the Horten brothers.\n- Late in World War II, Reimar Horten and Walter Horten initially designed the Horten H.IX as a German prototype fighter-bomber.\n- The RLM designation for the Horten H.IX was Ho 229.\n- The name Gotha Go 229 referred to the Ho 229 when extensive redesign work by Gotha prepared the aircraft for mass production.\n- Gothaer Waggonfabrik was to build the Horten H.IX.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "251bef20-ae9b-597c-b4fe-36a1b093895f",
        "text": "Page: Horten Ho 229. Sentence: The Horten H.IX, RLM designation Ho 229 (or Gotha Go 229 for extensive re-design work done by Gotha to prepare the aircraft for mass production) was a German prototype fighter/bomber initially designed by Reimar and Walter Horten to be built by Gothaer Waggonfabrik late in World War II.\nPage: Horten brothers. Sentence: Walter Horten (born 13 November 1913; died 9 December 1998 in Baden-Baden, Germany) and Reimar Horten (born 12 March 1915; died 14 March 1994 in Villa General Belgrano, Argentina), sometimes credited as the Horten Brothers, were German aircraft pilots and enthusiasts.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
